meta {
  name: Update Page/Form Org Mapping
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/page-org-map/{{mappingId}}?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "org_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "is_active": true
  }
}

docs {
  Reassigns a mapping to a different branch, or disables it. Requires
  super_admin. Both fields are optional (COALESCE semantics server-side).

  Regression checks:
    * mappingId belonging to ANOTHER tenant -> 404, NOT 204. Before this phase
      the statement had no RETURNING and no row-count check, so RLS filtered the
      row out, the UPDATE matched nothing, and the API answered 204 as though
      the edit had been applied.
    * mappingId that does not exist at all  -> 404, the same answer. The two are
      indistinguishable on purpose: telling them apart would confirm the
      existence of another tenant's row.
    * caller below super_admin              -> 403
}
